---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";

export const title = "Tour de Lopez 2026";
export const date = "2026-04-25";
export const excerpt = "An annual bike ride on Lopez Island — 30 miles, 9 people, one campsite on the beach, and a ferry that made an unscheduled stop for someone who almost didn't make it.";
export const tags = ["cycling", "san-juan-islands", "camping", "washington"];
const description =
  "An annual bike ride on Lopez Island: 30 miles, 9 people, one campsite on the beach, and a ferry that made an unscheduled stop for someone who almost didn't make it.";
---

<SiteLayout title={`${title} — Saachi K Gupta`} description={description} ogImage="/images/lopez/ride.jpg">
  <h1>{title}</h1>
  <p style="opacity:0.7; font-size: 13px;">{date}</p>

  <p style="max-width: 75ch;">
    Tour de Lopez is an annual community bike ride on Lopez Island in the San Juans — flat roads, beautiful views, a campsite on the beach. My friends and I did it for the first time in 2025 and I couldn't wait to return. In 2025, there were nine of us, and I organized it, which mostly meant making a group chat and booking the campsite.
  </p>

  <figure>
    <img
      src="/images/lopez/registration.jpg"
      alt="At the Tour de Lopez registration tent on a sunny April morning"
      style="border-radius: 8px;"
    />
    <figcaption>Registration. The ride starts here.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h2 style="margin-top: 28px;">The Peter saga</h2>

  <p style="max-width: 75ch;">
    The ferry from Anacortes to Lopez Island is the only way onto the island (save flying in or your own boat). We planned for an after-work ferry, and barely made it on.
  </p>

  <p style="max-width: 75ch;">
    However, one of my friends did not. He did eventually make it (many hours later) thanks to an unscheduled stop at Lopez by a later ferry.
    </p>



  <h2 style="margin-top: 28px;">The ride</h2>

  <p style="max-width: 75ch;">
    30 miles, all road, no gravel. Lopez is flat enough that it's genuinely enjoyable rather than just hard. We rode through farmland, past water, through tiny towns. The island has maybe 2,500 people and feels like it's been the same for 40 years.
  </p>

  <figure>
    <img loading="lazy"
      src="/images/lopez/ride.jpg"
      alt="Two of us in bike helmets at a scenic water overlook, thumbs up, deep blue water behind"
      style="border-radius: 8px;"
    />
    <figcaption>Somewhere on the 30-mile loop. Thumbs up warranted.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h2 style="margin-top: 28px;">The campsite</h2>

  <p style="max-width: 75ch;">
    We camped right on the beach. Dinner was at a picnic table facing the water during golden hour — wine, chips, many snacks, and TIRAMISU.
  </p>

  <figure>
    <img loading="lazy"
      src="/images/lopez/campsite-dinner.jpg"
      alt="Four of us at a picnic table on the beach at golden hour, water and mountains behind"
      style="border-radius: 8px;"
    />
  </figure>

  <figure>
    <img loading="lazy"
      src="/images/lopez/sunset.jpg"
      alt="Lopez Island sunset — deep purple and pink over the water, forest silhouette"
      style="border-radius: 8px;"
    />
    <figcaption>The Lopez sunset is genuinely something.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <figure>
    <img loading="lazy"
      src="/images/lopez/campfire.jpg"
      alt="Two people at the campfire, roasting a hot dog on a stick"
      style="border-radius: 8px;"
    />
    <figcaption> After riding, we returned to camp to warm up, grill, and enjoy another sunset. </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h2 style="margin-top: 28px;">After Lopez</h2>

  <p style="max-width: 75ch;">
    The ferry back passes through Anacortes, which puts you 20 minutes from the Skagit Valley tulip fields. This year we didn't treat it as a side trip. We actually planned around it, stayed for the afternoon, and wandered through the rows. Third year in a row going. It's become part of the weekend.
  </p>

  <p style="max-width: 75ch;">
    My Strava route from the ride: <a href="https://www.strava.com/routes/3350949975691107732" target="_blank" rel="noopener">strava.com/routes/3350949975691107732</a>
  </p>

</SiteLayout>
